From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: b43: AP mode: hold frames for stations in power save

b43 did nothing for dozing stations in AP mode: sta_notify was empty and
the ucode's power-management queue interrupt is drained and ignored. mac80211
buffers new frames for a dozing station itself, but frames already handed to
the driver were sent to a station that does not listen, re-sent until the
retry limit and dropped. A phone in power save lost 10-25 % of the pings
under load.

mac80211 re-buffers frames that come back with IEEE80211_TX_STAT_TX_FILTERED,
except A-MPDU frames, which it frees. So, as ath9k does, the driver keeps
them:
- sta_notify(SLEEP) marks the station; the TX work moves its frames from the
  TX queue to a per-station queue, and an A-MPDU frame that comes back
  without block ack while the station dozes goes there too (it keeps its
  place in the block ack window and its retry count).
- ieee80211_sta_set_buffered() reports the TIDs that hold frames, so the TIM
  bit is set.
- sta_notify(AWAKE): the held frames go back to the head of the TX queue,
  before what mac80211 buffered meanwhile.
- release_buffered_frames: the frames for a PS-Poll or uAPSD trigger go out
  with MoreData/EOSP set; a released frame the station did not take is held
  again and ends the service period.
- A plain (non-aggregated) frame that was not acked while its station dozes
  goes back to mac80211 as filtered.
The queue heads are only changed with wl->mutex held (TX work, TX status);
sta_notify and release_buffered_frames run in atomic context and only set
flags. Nothing changes while no station dozes. debugfs b43_ampdu shows
"ps held/filtered/released/resumed".

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
index 5558ac6..80abe6b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
@@ -932,6 +932,11 @@ struct b43_ampdu_stats {
 	u32 ack_tries[6];	/* acked frames by earlier driver re-sends (0..5) */
 	u32 notack[4];		/* not acked: no BA / bit 0 in window / behind BA SSN / >= 64 ahead */
 	u32 drop_cause[4];	/* finally dropped, same causes as notack */
+	/* AP power save */
+	u32 ps_held;		/* frames held for a dozing station */
+	u32 ps_filtered;	/* plain frames given back to mac80211 as filtered */
+	u32 ps_released;	/* held frames released for a PS-Poll/uAPSD */
+	u32 ps_resumed;		/* held frames sent after the station woke */
 };
 
